# How to cite this package. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo uses it for the DOI of each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "golemcrypto: Interactive Cryptocurrency Time Series and Market Data Explorer"
abstract: "A 'shiny' application for exploring cryptocurrency exchange rates. Plots interactive candlestick and volume charts of historical prices since 2013 for any active cryptocurrency, and shows a table of the top 100 cryptocurrencies by market capitalisation with price changes over 24 hours to 90 days, market dominance and fully diluted market cap, with Bollinger bands and the relative strength index on the price charts. Also compares normalized prices of several coins, on their own or relative to one of them, and shows a market cap treemap, a calendar of monthly returns, their seasonality by day of the week, week of the year, month, year of the halving cycle and calendar effects such as the turn of the month, whether a coin's recent volatility is normal, with a GARCH forecast, and its falls from its all-time high. Market data is retrieved from 'CoinMarketCap'."
authors:
  - family-names: "Zacharatos"
    given-names: "Dimitrios"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1789-8294"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sedzinfo/golemcrypto"
url: "https://sedzinfo.github.io/golemcrypto/"
keywords:
  - "golem"
  - "shiny"
  - "bitcoin"
  - "cryptocurrency"
  - "data-visualization"
  - "time-series"
